# Authentication

Scope: `implesia-mart-backend` only.

Auth stays Bearer JWT. Do not put the access token in a cookie. If a cookie session is ever added, CSRF protection is required on every cookie-authenticated unsafe method.

- Access tokens stay short-lived (minutes, not days).
- Refresh tokens rotate: accepting a refresh issues a new pair and invalidates the presented refresh token. Reuse of an old refresh token revokes that session.
- Logout revokes the refresh token. A revoked token cannot mint a new access token.
- Login, refresh, and logout are rate limited tighter than the default API limit. Repeated failures back off. See `rate-limiting.mdc`.
- Password checks use the existing bcrypt path. Do not compare password hashes with `==`.
- Responses and logs never include the password, the hash, or the raw token.
